WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.980
<b>Tower, First Floor: Colorless Garden</b>

00:07.820 --> 00:11.410
<b>Clairie's House
Secret Base for Single Witches</b>

00:12.960 --> 00:14.690
U-Um...

00:16.130 --> 00:20.120
Why am I half-naked now?

00:16.830 --> 00:20.120
<b>Will Serfort</b>

00:20.380 --> 00:24.880
It's fine, it's fine! 
I won't do anything bad.

00:25.220 --> 00:29.260
You... So you <i>do</i>
 have appalling proclivities!

00:25.340 --> 00:29.090
<b>Julius Reinberg</b>

00:29.620 --> 00:33.030
You misunderstand me! This is necessary.

00:33.030 --> 00:36.110
So let's lower those hands, 
shall we, Will?

00:36.640 --> 00:38.020
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:38.280 --> 00:42.050
How is this a misunderstanding? 
You are a bona fide pervert of a witch!

00:45.660 --> 00:48.280
<i>What are those scars?</i>

00:49.340 --> 00:51.510
<i>I'd heard rumors, but...</i>

00:51.510 --> 00:55.420
<i>Just how much insanity did he put 
himself through to ascend to the tower?</i>

00:55.910 --> 00:57.990
Yes, indeed.

00:58.590 --> 00:59.410
Will.

01:00.760 --> 01:04.420
Where and how did you 
get this scar on your back?

01:04.890 --> 01:09.420
Um, I think I got it while protecting 
Elfie when we were little.

01:09.860 --> 01:11.650
I see.

01:11.650 --> 01:12.950
This is probably it, then.

01:12.950 --> 01:13.920
Ow!

01:14.520 --> 01:17.700
Um, what are you doing?

01:17.700 --> 01:22.110
I was ascertaining the location 
of the lock to open the next door.

01:22.440 --> 01:26.190
<b>Cerridwen</b>

01:23.190 --> 01:26.190
I was watching the two of you train.

01:27.060 --> 01:30.850
Focusing on anchoring 
was a very smart choice.

01:30.850 --> 01:35.210
If Will can control the magical energy 
he anchors, it will lead him to Wis.

01:35.210 --> 01:37.070
That line of thinking is correct.

01:38.060 --> 01:41.280
Though I think it'd be best if you 
were a little more honest with yourself.

01:41.880 --> 01:44.710
You really are brilliant, 
aren't you, Julius?

01:44.710 --> 01:47.300
I don't need your empty flattery.

01:47.300 --> 01:49.960
I was wrong, wasn't I?

01:50.390 --> 01:52.340
You weren't wrong.

01:52.340 --> 01:54.900
Will is the very embodiment of anchoring.

01:54.900 --> 01:58.670
The truth is that he's already cleared 
the hurdle of storing magical energy.

01:59.290 --> 02:03.640
Because Will has the blood of mages, 
of wands, running through his veins.

02:05.190 --> 02:07.980
But Will's body is a little bit unique.

02:08.370 --> 02:10.820
He can't <i>expel</i>
 magical energy from himself.

02:10.820 --> 02:13.830
Instead, he greedily 
hoards it all deep, deep inside.

02:14.340 --> 02:17.100
No matter how much his body may scream,

02:17.100 --> 02:20.580
he consumes magical energy 
from without and stores it.

02:20.850 --> 02:22.000
I store it?

02:22.500 --> 02:25.200
Your assignment is now to learn

02:25.200 --> 02:28.360
how to draw on that stored energy at will.

02:28.360 --> 02:32.440
In other words, 
to charge yourself on your own.

02:32.860 --> 02:36.030
That is the next stage 
you should try to reach.

02:36.030 --> 02:37.860
H-Hold on.

02:37.860 --> 02:42.520
I thought I needed other people,
 external spells, in order to charge.

02:42.520 --> 02:45.270
That's correct, but it's not all.

02:45.860 --> 02:47.660
As proof, you've activated powers

02:47.660 --> 02:51.750
other than the spells 
you've charged with, haven't you?

02:54.030 --> 02:56.530
What you'll be doing now 
is putting <i>that</i> to use.

02:57.750 --> 03:01.900
By recalling the story of this magic 
linked through your blood and memories,

03:01.900 --> 03:05.040
you'll be able to charge up on your own.

03:05.650 --> 03:09.790
Without relying on the magic of others, 
it will be a new kind of charge.

03:10.570 --> 03:12.800
A new kind of charge?

03:13.420 --> 03:15.300
It is the power of emotions.

03:19.230 --> 03:22.720
Starting now, I will pour 
my power into the lock

03:22.720 --> 03:25.060
and guide you to a certain place.

03:25.550 --> 03:29.560
There, you must remember. 
Remember your roots.

03:29.950 --> 03:34.520
Then carve that into your body. 
Engrave the means to recall it.

03:35.530 --> 03:37.220
Herein lies the oath.

03:37.710 --> 03:40.820
Hide the forbidden true name of the blade
and trace the esteemed bloodline.

03:41.490 --> 03:43.410
Herein lies the keyhole.

03:43.410 --> 03:47.080
Borrow the honored name 
of the witch, and now open the story.

03:50.990 --> 03:52.040
Unlock.

03:54.510 --> 03:56.210
Twarv Historia!

03:58.640 --> 04:00.480
Come back safely, Will.

04:11.810 --> 04:13.110
<i>These are...</i>

04:14.050 --> 04:15.870
<i>all my memories!</i>

04:36.260 --> 04:37.800
Ow...

04:38.310 --> 04:39.540
What just happened?

04:39.540 --> 04:40.760
Will!

04:41.150 --> 04:43.210
Are you all right?!

04:43.870 --> 04:44.760
Here!

04:45.470 --> 04:47.810
The forest is dangerous, 
so let's hold hands.

04:49.650 --> 04:51.970
Elfie?

04:52.580 --> 04:56.190
I'll protect you, Will!

05:12.040 --> 05:16.750
Episode 21
The Page to Be Turned

06:28.350 --> 06:30.450
Hey! What's going on?

06:30.790 --> 06:34.870
<b>Clairie's House
Secret Base for Single Witches, Bedroom</b>

06:30.950 --> 06:33.100
It's been four days 
since he lost consciousness,

06:33.100 --> 06:34.960
and he hasn't opened his eyes once!

06:35.430 --> 06:38.710
He's diving deep into his dreams.

06:39.700 --> 06:42.290
My magic has given him an opportunity.

06:42.290 --> 06:44.720
He's in the midst of recalling his past.

06:44.720 --> 06:47.460
Dreams? His past?

06:47.460 --> 06:52.980
Is remembering things like that really 
going to help him obtain this new power?

06:53.680 --> 06:56.760
I'm a teensy bit unsure myself.

06:56.760 --> 06:58.780
After all, swords are Finn's jurisdiction.

06:58.780 --> 06:59.480
Seriously?!

07:01.190 --> 07:03.880
I have no intention 
of disputing Finn's methods.

07:04.240 --> 07:05.410
However...

07:05.410 --> 07:10.240
when it comes to commanding the heavens, 
I think there are other approaches.

07:11.630 --> 07:13.000
What are you talking about?

07:13.860 --> 07:16.630
History fills your body,

07:17.320 --> 07:20.750
the traces of continued relations 
between wand and sword...

07:21.180 --> 07:23.390
Follow them back in time...

07:23.390 --> 07:25.010
All the way to your origins.

07:25.680 --> 07:27.430
And, if possible...

07:28.010 --> 07:32.060
I hope one day you may reach the Source.

07:35.870 --> 07:39.150
<i>My hands and feet are small.</i>

07:39.620 --> 07:40.670
<i>And...</i>

07:42.170 --> 07:43.780
<i>Elfie is, too!</i>

07:43.780 --> 07:45.410
What's wrong, Will?

07:46.340 --> 07:49.610
<i>It's like I've gone back in time.</i>

07:51.100 --> 07:54.910
<i>Am I really in the past?</i>

07:55.240 --> 07:58.420
<i>Does her magic reverse time?</i>

07:58.420 --> 08:03.670
<i>No. No matter how amazing her powers 
may be, no one can travel to the past.</i>

08:04.230 --> 08:07.290
<i>In that case, is this...</i>

08:04.520 --> 08:05.440
Hey.

08:05.440 --> 08:06.330
Hey!

08:06.330 --> 08:07.430
Will?

08:07.290 --> 08:10.720
<i>Am I being shown the past 
through something like a dream?</i>

08:07.460 --> 08:09.720
Hey! Will?

08:11.960 --> 08:14.200
Look at me!

08:15.490 --> 08:19.980
Will, you were thinking of 
some other girl, weren't you?

08:19.980 --> 08:21.460
What? No, I wasn't!

08:21.460 --> 08:25.700
But at home, you're always being 
nice to Claire and the others!

08:25.700 --> 08:28.960
That's only because I'm helping Father!

08:28.960 --> 08:30.360
You can't!

08:30.360 --> 08:33.420
I won't forgive you if you cheat on me!

08:31.780 --> 08:33.550
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

08:33.420 --> 08:39.080
You can't! Not ever, Will! 
I don't want you to cheat on me!

08:33.550 --> 08:38.080
<i>Elfaria was even more selfish
 back then than she is now.</i>

08:38.640 --> 08:41.920
Elfie, what can I do so you'll forgive me?

08:39.080 --> 08:41.920
I hate this!

08:43.090 --> 08:44.770
Hug me!

08:52.320 --> 08:54.240
And pat my head, too.

08:54.240 --> 08:55.440
There you go.

09:01.310 --> 09:03.380
<i>This is so nostalgic.</i>

09:03.380 --> 09:07.730
<i>Back then, she was always getting me
to soothe her like this.</i>

09:10.430 --> 09:15.770
All right! I've refilled on Will power, 
so let's go defeat some monsters!

09:16.280 --> 09:19.250
E-Elfie! Did you say defeat monsters?

09:19.830 --> 09:22.580
They say there's a strange 
monster in the forest.

09:22.580 --> 09:26.500
It's causing problems for Father, 
so let's you and me take it down, Will!

09:26.500 --> 09:29.460
What? But that's dangerous!

09:30.200 --> 09:34.760
Elfie, you're amazing, 
but I can't use magic at all.

09:35.380 --> 09:36.940
<i>My voice is coming out on its own!</i>

09:37.340 --> 09:41.020
<i>Because this is the past, 
am I following what I said back then?</i>

09:43.590 --> 09:48.360
Don't worry! I brought the book we love!

09:48.970 --> 09:52.530
Just having this fills us 
with courage, doesn't it?

09:53.060 --> 09:54.830
Like whoosh!

09:54.830 --> 09:56.660
So we'll be just fine!

09:57.510 --> 09:59.880
I'll protect you, Will!

10:01.410 --> 10:02.770
<i>That's right.</i>

10:03.450 --> 10:07.070
<i>The old me was a scaredy-cat and a coward.</i>

10:07.070 --> 10:10.200
<i>And because I was like that, 
Elfie was always protecting me.</i>

10:15.060 --> 10:19.810
<i>When was it that she
 started depending on me?</i>

10:31.990 --> 10:33.170
Time for a break!

10:33.790 --> 10:35.690
And now...

10:35.690 --> 10:38.330
some amazing magic I thought up!

10:38.810 --> 10:40.680
Isnomee Lasli!

10:45.390 --> 10:47.580
Here, Will! It's for you!

10:49.020 --> 10:50.750
Thanks, Elfie!

10:53.550 --> 10:56.780
<i>The second secret magic 
that Elfaria invented...</i>

10:56.780 --> 11:00.350
<i>was a gentle spell 
that only created ice candies.</i>

11:03.590 --> 11:06.100
<i>I loved those ice candies.</i>

11:06.830 --> 11:08.860
This is a secret from 
Claire and the others.

11:09.210 --> 11:10.060
Yeah!

11:11.510 --> 11:15.670
Elfie, why do you give me 
so many ice candies?

11:15.670 --> 11:21.070
Because you're always sharing your food
 with everyone at the orphanage.

11:21.550 --> 11:22.620
And...

11:23.140 --> 11:27.620
if you eat lots of them, 
then you'll be full of me, right?

11:28.470 --> 11:29.480
Yeah!

11:29.480 --> 11:30.630
That's true.

11:31.260 --> 11:35.840
Now, before our adventure, 
let's fill ourselves with powerful energy!

11:35.840 --> 11:37.930
I'll do the reading again today.

11:38.510 --> 11:41.890
I'm sorry I can't read yet.

11:41.890 --> 11:43.640
No, it's fine!

11:46.180 --> 11:47.740
<i></i>The Adventures of Deimne<i>.</i>

11:48.230 --> 11:50.120
<i>Elfie loved it.</i>

11:50.120 --> 11:52.840
<i>It was why we made a promise 
to see the sunset together.</i>

11:52.840 --> 11:54.100
<i>That book was precious to us.</i>

11:54.730 --> 11:56.480
<i>It really takes me back.</i>

11:56.480 --> 11:58.840
The mean witch said,

11:59.180 --> 12:00.180
"You see?"

12:00.180 --> 12:04.290
"This crimson treasure, more beautiful than
any other in the world, doesn't exist!"

12:04.780 --> 12:07.040
"All of that was just your blatant lies!"

12:07.760 --> 12:10.290
The impertinent hero replied,

12:10.290 --> 12:13.780
"It seems the sky is in a bad mood today."

12:13.780 --> 12:17.300
"Just wait a bit. 
I'll go and have a word."

12:17.700 --> 12:21.790
When the hero drew his sword, 
the gray sky split,

12:21.790 --> 12:25.560
revealing the most beautiful 
crimson in the world.

12:26.070 --> 12:28.260
<i>Wait. This illustration...</i>

12:28.260 --> 12:32.240
<i>I never noticed before, 
but it sort of looks like... Mister Finn.</i>

12:33.090 --> 12:39.230
Captivated by a sunset unmatched
 by any treasure, the witch cried.

12:40.150 --> 12:41.820
And then what happened?

12:45.470 --> 12:47.830
<i>Maybe I'm imagining it.</i>

12:48.340 --> 12:52.940
After a long journey, the witch said,

12:52.940 --> 12:56.360
"In order to see that sunset again..."

12:57.710 --> 12:58.810
Will?

12:59.970 --> 13:01.550
Did you get sleepy?

13:01.550 --> 13:03.340
Yeah. Sorry.

13:03.340 --> 13:04.220
It's fine!

13:04.680 --> 13:07.870
I'm sorry for waking you up so soon.

13:11.340 --> 13:13.690
Today, I'll let you use 
my lap as a pillow!

13:15.480 --> 13:16.940
Come on. Lie down.

13:19.580 --> 13:24.700
<i>This peaceful everyday life with 
just us two... I want to go back to that.</i>

13:25.270 --> 13:28.560
<i>I wonder if it's wrong to feel that way.</i>

13:44.640 --> 13:45.470
<i>Huh?</i>

13:45.470 --> 13:47.350
<i>What? Elfie?</i>

13:47.350 --> 13:48.270
<i>Miss Elfie?!</i>

13:48.270 --> 13:49.680
<i>What are you trying to do?!</i>

13:49.680 --> 13:51.230
<i>Hey! Hang on!</i>

13:53.910 --> 13:55.980
Morning, Elfie.

13:56.460 --> 13:57.680
What were you doing?

13:57.680 --> 13:59.370
N-N-Nothing!

13:59.370 --> 14:03.240
Y-You had something on your face, Will, 
so I was going to take it off for you.

14:03.600 --> 14:05.030
That's all it was.

14:05.030 --> 14:07.280
Why are you talking so weirdly?

14:07.760 --> 14:09.340
L-Let's get going!

14:09.340 --> 14:11.870
Time to protect the peace of the forest!

14:10.680 --> 14:11.870
E-Elfie!

14:12.510 --> 14:16.960
<i>The next time I see Elfie, 
I don't know how I'll face her.</i>

14:30.530 --> 14:33.600
There's war in this place called Rigarden,

14:33.600 --> 14:36.560
and they say bad people and monsters 
are running from there.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.120
Really?

14:38.120 --> 14:40.990
Yeah. That's why the monsters

14:40.990 --> 14:44.070
came to the forest from Rigarden 
and are doing bad things!

14:44.710 --> 14:46.050
Monsters?

14:46.660 --> 14:48.410
<i>I'm starting to remember.</i>

14:48.410 --> 14:51.330
<i>Ten years ago, Elfie and I came here...</i>

14:51.780 --> 14:54.880
<i>We came to this forest behind 
the orphanage, just the two of us.</i>

14:55.390 --> 14:58.570
<i>Father said we shouldn't go there, though.</i>

15:00.210 --> 15:02.620
B-But you'll be fine, right, Elfie?

15:02.620 --> 15:04.190
Leave it to me!

15:04.850 --> 15:07.190
<i>I'm certain we had this conversation.</i>

15:07.710 --> 15:10.890
<i>But my memory of what comes next is hazy.</i>

15:11.540 --> 15:14.660
<i>Just what happened after this?</i>

15:31.070 --> 15:31.870
<i>That's...</i>

15:38.670 --> 15:41.880
<b><u>Will in His Youth</u>

Tenderhearted and hardworking, he is the oldest at the orphanage and often required to practice self-restraint, but he never shows disgruntlement.
On the one hand, that's extremely helpful, but on the other, it makes me feel like a failure as an adult. 
He seems to have developed a complex about being unable to use magic.
But, and I feel bad for Will for saying this, I simply don't think he has that special power in him.
That boy is far too different. If it were possible, I'd like to stay by his side to watch over him forever. May the blessing of the Mage Queen be with him.

-Excerpt from the diary of Ashley Serfort, foster father</b>

15:43.670 --> 15:46.880
<b><u>Elfaria in Her Youth</u>

A mischievous natural-born leader, she is infatuated with Will, and I can never predict what she might get up to.
 On top of that, her magical skill already easily exceeds my own, so I cannot control her at all.
I suspect that Elfaria will cause a revolution in our world of magic, but if by chance Will isn't there, then...
She'd make the whole world her enemy. I have no doubt about that.
Will, please look after her. I beg you. I'm sorry I'm such a powerless foster father.

-Excerpt from the diary of Ashley Serfort, foster father</b>

15:47.800 --> 15:49.030
A wolf?

15:49.390 --> 15:52.640
No... a crystal monster?

15:53.510 --> 15:54.890
<i>That's no monster.</i>

15:55.190 --> 15:56.390
<i>I know what it is now.</i>

15:57.080 --> 15:59.900
<i>That's a mage-created creature!</i>

16:00.220 --> 16:01.820
<i>It's been injured?</i>

16:02.260 --> 16:04.740
<i>Is it really a solitary unit 
that fled the war?</i>

16:07.470 --> 16:08.860
Will, stay here!

16:08.860 --> 16:09.820
Elfie!

16:10.550 --> 16:12.580
I'll kill this thing!

16:15.300 --> 16:18.490
I've thought up an amazing magic!

16:23.520 --> 16:25.090
Ars Weiss!

16:25.090 --> 16:29.090
Me and a whole bunch of other 
mes are gonna beat you up!

16:31.070 --> 16:33.550
<i>She's multicasting Ars Weiss!</i>

16:33.550 --> 16:36.080
<i>She's had this level of control 
since she was a child!</i>

16:36.080 --> 16:38.100
<i>Elfie really is incredible!</i>

16:39.280 --> 16:41.100
<i>But wait...</i>

16:41.380 --> 16:44.360
<i>Why do I feel so uneasy?</i>

16:45.370 --> 16:47.220
Here we go!

16:47.220 --> 16:49.110
Tearis Nono!

16:52.370 --> 16:54.280
Elfie! Run!

16:54.870 --> 16:55.620
What?

16:58.170 --> 16:59.870
Elfie! El—

17:03.900 --> 17:07.380
<i>That creature has the special ability 
to reflect magic!</i>

17:08.350 --> 17:10.970
Run! Run, Elfie!

17:10.970 --> 17:12.790
It doesn't hurt.

17:12.790 --> 17:15.140
I'm not scared!

17:15.140 --> 17:18.390
Because I'm going to take you down!

17:19.640 --> 17:22.900
Because I'm going to protect Will!

17:26.460 --> 17:27.760
<i>I can't move.</i>

17:28.830 --> 17:31.700
<i>It's my fault that Elfie is...</i>

17:32.770 --> 17:37.290
<i>You can't be serious! 
Move! Run! Get out there!</i>

17:37.880 --> 17:40.950
<i>The version of you 
always being saved by Elfie</i>

17:40.950 --> 17:42.790
<i>is who you hate more than anything!</i>

17:43.550 --> 17:46.040
<i>Go! Go now!</i>

17:46.330 --> 17:47.680
<i>Go!</i>

18:03.350 --> 18:06.630
What? Will...

18:09.140 --> 18:11.610
No!

18:11.980 --> 18:13.860
Will? Will?!

18:13.860 --> 18:16.300
Stay with me! Will! Will!

18:16.300 --> 18:17.480
<i>That's right.</i>

18:17.950 --> 18:20.600
<i>I protected Elfie...</i>

18:21.150 --> 18:23.800
<i>and then I lost consciousness.</i>

18:25.460 --> 18:27.840
<i>What happened after that?</i>

18:27.840 --> 18:29.890
<i>Did someone rescue Elfie?</i>

18:32.180 --> 18:34.290
<i>But who?</i>

18:42.630 --> 18:43.770
Awaken.

18:49.870 --> 18:52.390
<i>My body... feels hot.</i>

18:52.390 --> 18:54.780
<i>I'm going to explode!</i>

18:54.780 --> 18:58.030
<i>I'm turning into a sword!</i>

18:59.090 --> 19:00.290
Will?

19:01.320 --> 19:03.040
<i>That's right.</i>

19:05.880 --> 19:08.040
<i>There's more to the story.</i>

19:08.460 --> 19:09.880
<i>This adventure...</i>

19:11.750 --> 19:14.810
<i>was the beginning of the sword.</i>

19:19.910 --> 19:21.640
Fully charged...

19:26.310 --> 19:27.990
Tearis Wis!

19:38.430 --> 19:40.280
<i>I finally understand.</i>

19:40.750 --> 19:45.160
<i>I know why, back then, 
I thought this power was unstoppable.</i>

19:46.370 --> 19:48.290
<i>It's because I knew!</i>

19:48.830 --> 19:51.170
<i>I knew what Elfie's power had created...</i>

19:51.820 --> 19:53.050
<i>I knew this mageblade!</i>

19:57.630 --> 19:58.380
Will!

20:24.990 --> 20:26.970
So that's what it was.

20:27.670 --> 20:31.320
This is your magic, Will.

20:35.190 --> 20:38.030
<i>This was my beginning.</i>

20:38.700 --> 20:40.380
<i>These precious feelings...</i>

20:42.440 --> 20:43.990
<i>I won't forget them again.</i>

20:45.470 --> 20:48.920
<i>I'll always remember this bond 
I have with Elfie!</i>

20:49.430 --> 20:51.890
Thank you, Will.

20:58.990 --> 21:01.850
Hey! Are you awake?

21:01.850 --> 21:03.120
Julius?

21:03.400 --> 21:06.310
Hurry up! You've been asleep for six days!

21:06.310 --> 21:08.400
The Second Bloom is about to start!

21:10.320 --> 21:12.550
Hey! Are you listening?

21:12.550 --> 21:14.130
Hurry up!

21:14.860 --> 21:17.220
The magical energy you've anchored...

21:17.220 --> 21:19.630
Did you manage to grasp the nature
of what's inside you?

21:21.450 --> 21:22.890
Yes, I have.

21:23.580 --> 21:26.890
Do you think you'll be able to 
recall the paths you've walked?

21:27.760 --> 21:29.140
Anytime!

21:38.650 --> 21:40.440
Then go.

21:40.440 --> 21:43.010
Go and write a new story!

21:43.010 --> 21:43.920
I will!

23:27.970 --> 23:30.930
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

23:36.670 --> 23:39.110
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.490 --> 23:44.280
episode 22,
 "Hoping, Blooming, Thundering."

23:40.400 --> 23:45.900
Episode 22
Hoping, Blooming, Thundering
